[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[4A\r\u001b[J\r\nBoth pieces are done and the suite passes: 7 tests, run with \u001b[36mpython3\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m-m\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36munittest\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m-v\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mmode()\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1min\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mstats.py\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m returns the most frequent value. On a tie it returns the smallest tied value,\r\n  and it raises \u001b[36mValueError\u001b[0m on empty input. I added three tests in \u001b[36mtest_stats.py\u001b[0m for a clear mode, a\r\n  tie, and the empty-input error.\r\n\u001b[2m\u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36mREADME.md\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m new file that describes the four functions, gives a usage example, and says how to run\r\n  the tests. I ran its examples against the code and they give the stated results.\r\n\r\nLimits:\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u2022 \u001b[0m\u001b[36mmode()\u001b[0m needs hashable values, so a list of lists would fail. The other functions do not have this\r\n  limit.\r\n\u001b[2m\u2022 \u001b[0mNothing is committed. \u001b[36mstats.py\u001b[0m and \u001b[36mtest_stats.py\u001b[0m are modified, and \u001b[36mREADME.md\u001b[0m is untracked.\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500 Worked for 15s \u00b7 8 turns \u00b7 $0.0040 "]
